UNIT carried_shape_type
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 ae3eb92884f1cf9748eec04427b895efcd25660f5114e7aa89ba40b83692debe
SIG export default function carried_shape_type(shape: string): Json
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime and is driven exactly as js. Declare in the artifact
  type Json = null | boolean | number | string | readonly Json[] | { readonly [key: string]: Json }
  (the abstract json; no undefined anywhere). text = string (UTF-16). The result is the TREE node: a node = a plain object
  (k, item, key, val, items, alts, fields), a list = an array, a record field = a two-element array [name, node]. STRICT:
  the artifact type-checks under strict: true with no any, no non-null assertions (!), no @ts-ignore and no
  @ts-expect-error. A throw (R2 empty or arrow-led K, R3, R5–R8) is a thrown Error; the message is not graded. ES
  module default export; imports nothing.
ENVELOPE as the primary; no widening is claimed.
MECHANISM (restated from js — language files are self-contained, not inherited) R1 = shape.split(';')[0]. WS (R2, R4,
  R5) is space, tab, CR and LF only: NOT String.prototype.trim and NOT \s, which also strip or match U+00A0, U+000B,
  U+000C, U+3000, U+FEFF and more. The pinned TRIM and ARROW regexes realize R2: the s flag lets . cross line breaks, and
  the lazy (.+?) makes K end at the FIRST arrow. R4 = the pinned WIDEN replace (global, no m flag: ^ and $ are the ends of
  the whole text) on the whole normalized text, keeping the matched left context and writing the sign letter followed by
  64. The reader (R5–R8) is a hand scan with the same WS. Read a word as a whole IDENT run, then classify it. A regex
  match group is string | undefined under strict: narrow it with a test, never with !.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex TRIM = /^[ \t\r\n]+|[ \t\r\n]+$/g CITED R2 — replaced by the empty text
PINNED regex ARROW = /^map[ \t\r\n]+(.+?)[ \t\r\n]*->[ \t\r\n]*(.+)$/s CITED R2 — groups 1 and 2 are K and V
PINNED regex WIDEN = /(^|[[,|:][ \t\r\n]*)([ui])(8|16|32)(?=[ \t\r\n]*(?:[\],|]|$))/g CITED R4 — group 1 kept, then group 2, then 64
PINNED regex IDENT = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/ CITED GRAMMAR IDENT
PROVENANCE rederive@6199e2cc8b75 cli/sir/v05.mjs carriedShapeType + cli/sir/canon.mjs reader. Language file re-cut
  2026-10-27 (round 5, delta 5b: one WS set, no > left context) with the primary, before any blind
  re-emission.
